From 39d00b365d2ce340dd8f0492141d387e8ce7732b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leandro Forain <leandro.forain@instructure.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:55:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] LeandrOS integration: crossterm fork, kill builtin,
 background job pids

- Cargo.toml: [patch.crates-io] crossterm = ../crossterm, the 0.29.0 fork
  that fixes the unix cursor-position-report request/response desync.
- kill: default signal is SIGTERM (POSIX/bash), numeric signal specs are
  accepted, and `kill -0` probes with signal 0 instead of failing.
- jobs: a background job run as an internal task publishes the pid of the
  first external process it spawns, so $!, jobs and kill %n have a pid.
